# detail
Number of changes: 1

1. Modified | Implementation code block
   Changed the body of `__invert__` from directly computing and wrapping an array to performing the computation and return in a `try-except` structure with additional exception-branch handling.
   The original implementation included:

   * Assignment statement: assign the result of `operator.inv(_values_from_object(self))` to `arr`;
   * Return statement: call and return `self._wrap_array(arr, self.axes, copy=False)`.

   The new implementation includes:

   * Try-except statement: in the `try` block, execute `operator.inv(_values_from_object(self))`, assign the result to `arr`, and then return `self.__array_wrap__(arr)`;
   * Conditional statement: in the `except` block, return `self` when `not np.prod(self.shape)` is true;
   * Raise statement: re-raise the exception at the end of the exception branch.
# /detail
# mode：Modify method implementation (add exception-handling structure and modify return-call statement)
